+# Final e-reader comparison
+
+## Verified comparison
+
+The corrected ceiling is $270 before tax. The retained rules are a warm-adjustable front light, IPX8 protection, at least 16 GB, and a U.S. public-library route. Screen size takes priority over low weight, while physical page-turn buttons remain a nice-to-have rather than a requirement.
+
+| Model | Listed price; display; weight | Required features | Controls and U.S. library route |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Kobo Libra Colour | $259.99; 7-inch color E Ink; 199.5 g; 32 GB [S1] | IPX8 and ComfortLight PRO with adjustable brightness and colour temperature [S1] | Physical page-turn buttons; direct OverDrive/Libby integration, subject to location and library availability [S1] |
+| Kobo Clara Colour | $179.99; 6-inch color E Ink; 174 g; 16 GB [S2] | IPX8 and ComfortLight PRO with adjustable brightness and colour temperature [S2] | Touchscreen documented, but physical buttons are not established; OverDrive/Libby integration is subject to location and library availability [S2] |
+| Kindle Paperwhite | $159.99 starting price; 7-inch display; 211 g; 16 GB [S3][S4][S5] | IPX8 and an adjustable warm light [S4] | Touch interaction is documented, but physical buttons are not established; compatible U.S. Libby loans use Read With Kindle and Amazon delivery [S3][S6] |
+
+All three stay under the corrected $270 budget and clear the four must-haves: each has at least 16 GB, an IPX8 rating, warm-light adjustment, and a documented U.S. library path. [S1][S2][S3][S4][S6] The two Kobo routes are integrated with OverDrive/Libby, whereas the Kindle Paperwhite route sends an eligible Libby loan through an Amazon account. [S1][S2][S6]
+
+The Kobo Libra Colour combines a seven-inch screen with the only physical page-turn buttons affirmatively documented in the pack, and it weighs 11.5 g less than the Kindle Paperwhite. [S1][S5] The Kobo Clara Colour is the lightest at 174 g, but its six-inch screen is smaller than both seven-inch alternatives. [S1][S2][S3][S5] Those are factual tradeoffs only; comfort in a particular hand is not established by dimensions or weight alone. [S1][S2][S3][S5]
+
+## Recommendation
+
+1. **Kobo Libra Colour** — Clear winner. Its seven-inch display fits the higher-priority screen preference, and its documented page-turn buttons supply the retained bonus. [S1] Its direct library integration and $259.99 price keep every must-have and the corrected budget intact. [S1]
+2. **Kindle Paperwhite** — Its seven-inch screen preserves the primary preference at the lowest listed starting price, while compatible Libby loans require an Amazon handoff and physical buttons are not established. [S3][S6] At 211 g, it is heavier than either Kobo. [S1][S2][S5]
+3. **Kobo Clara Colour** — Its direct library integration and 174 g weight are advantages, but its six-inch display loses because screen size outranks lightness. [S2] Physical page-turn buttons are not established. [S2]
+
+I would pick the Kobo Libra Colour because it wins on the corrected primary preference and uniquely confirms the buttons nice-to-have without sacrificing any must-have. [S1] That choice deliberately accepts a higher listed price and 25.5 g more weight than the Kobo Clara Colour; screen size is more important than low weight, though weight remains relevant. [S1][S2]
+
+## Uncertainties
+
+Prices can change, tax is excluded, and availability at the quoted starting prices is not established, so the Libra’s $10.01 cushion is not a delivered-price guarantee. [S1][S2][S3]
+
+Battery claims are not cleanly comparable because the supplied figures use different assumptions about daily reading, lighting, and radios; real endurance can vary with usage, so battery life did not determine the ranking. [S1][S2][S3][S4][S5]
+
+Library availability can vary by library and title: OverDrive is limited to select countries, while the Kindle route is U.S.-only and not every Libby book or library supplies Kindle format. [S1][S2][S6]
+
+Finally, handedness, grip comfort, and case weight are not given; although the sources establish device weights and some controls, an ergonomic winner remains unknown without handling the devices. [S1][S2][S3][S5]
